WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.560
A hand lifts a line from an old book and
sets it on the first page of a new one.

2
00:00:05.610 --> 00:00:09.770
In 1818, Frankenstein opens
with Adam's words to God,

3
00:00:09.820 --> 00:00:13.350
from Paradise Lost: "Did
I request thee, Maker,

4
00:00:13.400 --> 00:00:16.340
from my clay To mould me man?"

5
00:00:16.390 --> 00:00:18.920
Every story borrows from an older one.

6
00:00:18.970 --> 00:00:22.140
So is that theft, or conversation?

7
00:00:22.190 --> 00:00:25.130
In this mission, you'll
name the kinds of borrowing:

8
00:00:25.180 --> 00:00:28.850
allusion, epigraph, rewriting, parody.

9
00:00:28.900 --> 00:00:32.360
You'll look hard at why
Shelley chose Adam's question.

10
00:00:32.410 --> 00:00:36.900
And you'll read a Shakespeare sonnet that
borrows a whole tradition of love poems:

11
00:00:36.950 --> 00:00:41.070
"My mistress' eyes are nothing
like the sun;" Your mission:

12
00:00:41.120 --> 00:00:44.350
decide whether borrowing
is theft or conversation.
